  "findings": [
    "brain.model.add, brain.model.use and brain.ask ran end to end with real worker processes and the pinned CPU runtime; the model loaded in under a second and answered chat questions in 1.5 to 4.6 s.",
    "The first live reply exposed two defects fixed in this pass: an undefined name in the reply path (NameError) and a plan prompt larger than a 2,048-token context (CONTEXT_BUDGET_EXCEEDED); the plan prompt now carries a core set plus the tools chosen for the request.",
    "Plan mode returned schema-valid JSON but chose a poor operation (knowledge.page for a bold request); with 0.5B parameters the open proposal path is not a dependable decider.",
    "Choice mode (schema-constrained, temperature 0) answered deterministically but picked option 3 (read the page again) in every situation, including when 1 (sum) or 2 (units differ: ask) was plainly right. The loop therefore keeps explicit rules primary and treats the model pick as advisory, recorded as a step."
  ],
